        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of thiodiacylhydrazine (0.1 mmol, 10.6 mg), o-vanillin (0.1 mmol, 15.2 mg), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol, 90.2 mg) and triethylamine (15 μL) was dissolved in mixed solvent CH3OH:CH3CN = 1.3:0.7 (1.3 mL anhydrous methanol and 0.7 mL acetonitrile) in a PTFE reactor. The sealed reactor was heated at 80 °C in an oven for 2 days (48 h). After slow cooling to room temperature, yellow block crystals of complex 1 were obtained.",
